{"page":"RBPMS","gene":"RBPMS","accession":"Q93062","protein":"RNA-binding protein with multiple splicing","length":196,"events":["Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"Q93062-1","name":"A","synonyms":[],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"RNA binding protein that mediates the regulation of pre-mRNA alternative splicing (AS) (PubMed:24860013, PubMed:26347403). Acts either as activator (FLNB, HSPG2, LIPA1, MYOCD, PTPRF and PPFIBP1) or repressor (TPM1, ACTN1, ITGA7, PIEZO1, LSM14B, MBNL1 and MBML2) of splicing events on specific pre-mRNA targets (By similarity). Together with RNA binding proteins RBFOX2 and MBNL1/2, activates a splicing program associated with differentiated contractile vascular smooth muscle cells (SMC) by regulating AS of numerous pre-mRNA involved in actin cytoskeleton and focal adhesion machineries, suggesting a role in promoting a cell differentiated state (By similarity). Binds to introns, exons and 3'-UTR associated with tandem CAC trinucleotide motifs separated by a variable spacer region, at a minimum as a dimer. The minimal length of RNA required for RBPMS-binding tandem CAC motifs is 15 nt, with spacing ranging from 1 to 9 nt. Can also bind to CA dinucleotide repeats (PubMed:24860013, PubMed:26347403). Mediates repression of TPM1 exon 3 by binding to CAC tandem repeats in the flanking intronic regions, followed by higher-order oligomerization and heterotypic interactions with other splicing regulators including MBNL1 and RBFOX2, which prevents assembly of ATP-dependent splicing complexes (By similarity)"},{"topic":"Domain","text":"The C-terminal 20 amino acids region, without homology to other proteins, is essential for higher-order oligomerization (By similarity). Also essential for RBPMS cooperative RNA binding (By similarity)"},{"topic":"Miscellaneous","text":"May be produced at very low levels due to a premature stop codon in the mRNA, leading to nonsense-mediated mRNA decay"}],"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000397323.9","